{"id": "EUVD-2026-86653", "enisaUuid": "71ef3829-bc4c-36a7-b3a5-01af59b63c14", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: Fix potential UAF in pec_store\n\nSashiko reports:\n\nIn pec_store(), a guard(mutex)(&hwdev->lock) is taken. If the chip write\noperation returns an error other than -EOPNOTSUPP, the code jumps to the\nput label, which calls put_device(hdev). If this drops the final reference,\nthe device is freed. When the function then returns, the guard cleanup\nfunction runs and attempts to unlock the freed mutex.\n\nUse scoped_guard() instead of guard() to avoid the problem.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8afab57bcdbc2186f325972e777880ac5a220f4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01dd8b4fc2cf83c66565c0f382fb1841e9000a89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/354ccc99b2dc8ba0cf6d4de34e520bcf6ecca5c2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98000", "GHSA-xqgw-9m49-8xxh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ffc692e-f90b-3a10-a369-14c6018459df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "56145783-0ee2-3f4e-b47b-9fbe59530382", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "585ca9e8-37bb-3a89-ab27-ad64a4741454", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "5e909b99-7b86-3bf0-aeb6-67a471abc8c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3ad2a7b9b15d5072139a20be84adb36776eb6c9b <01dd8b4fc2cf83c66565c0f382fb1841e9000a89"}, {"id": "accdcd83-1089-3f0a-ad7a-9ad4e81b31bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "b674c852-aff7-3794-acc8-42bc47cd493a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3ad2a7b9b15d5